# Cockpit-unification patch for phantom-portal (the LAN cockpit adapter, lives outside this repo).
#
# WHY (architecture §9 the one contract + the one event bus, §12 multi-tenant event path):
# the deployed phantom-portal keeps its OWN second queue (~/.local/share/phantom-portal/jobs.db
# + an in-process worker loop) for "commissions", separate from pnd's governed queue. That means
# two queues, two records, two truths — and the portal's live views (/ws/feed room tail, /api/jobs
# poll) are NOT the typed event bus, so they can desync and carry no per-principal scoping. P2b
# closes this on the ENGINE side (typed `job_events` bus with per-principal topics + reconnect
# replay, a `subscribe` stream on the pnd socket, a single Canonical View Model, and the
# steer/approve/deny verbs). This patch lands the PORTAL side of the unification:
#
#   1. jobs.db is RETIRED. A commission becomes a pnd `task_type:commission.build` job (seeded in
#      pnlib/db.seed_v3): same single queue, same admission gating, same enforced Record, same
#      typed bus as every other job. POST /api/queue + /api/jobs submit commission.build with the
#      goal as a VETTED param (no shell concat); the new `_commission_goal` entrypoint runs the
#      build->review protocol INSIDE pnd's per-job workspace. The legacy jobs.db worker is not
#      started; delete jobs.db after applying:  rm ~/.local/share/phantom-portal/jobs.db
#   2. The portal points at the ONE event bus: a new /ws/events endpoint bridges the browser to
#      pnd's streaming `subscribe` verb (per-principal authorized SERVER-SIDE), and the queue tab
#      subscribes to it for realtime updates + reconnect replay (?after=<last_event_id>) instead
#      of pure polling. The Canonical View Model is surfaced on /api/queue/<id>.
#   3. The confirmation gate + steer reach the portal: /api/queue/approve (idempotent approve/deny
#      of a staged commission) and /api/queue/<id>/steer (live feedback into a running job).
#
# Because commission.build is needs_confirmation, a commission parks `staged` with a single-use
# nonce; the portal auto-approves on submit unless {"hold":true} is passed (then the operator
# confirms via /api/queue/approve). per-principal: the portal resolves a default topic
# (user/<principal>); pnd RE-RESOLVES the principal from peercred/broker and authorizes topics
# there, so the portal can never widen access. Full per-user web_users login is a later strand.
#
# This is a PORTAL-side + deploy-time change, delivered as an apply-during-maintenance-window
# patch (NOT applied live by this PR — no live deploy, no service restart). ORDER: apply
# phantom-portal-rce-removal.patch FIRST (or note the raw-cmd branch is already removed there;
# this patch's /api/queue POST also drops the raw path), then this one. Apply with:
#   cd ~/.local/bin && patch -p0 < /path/to/phantom-portal-cockpit-unification.patch
#   (the diff targets the bare file `phantom-portal`, so run it from ~/.local/bin)
# THEN: rm ~/.local/share/phantom-portal/jobs.db ; restart phantom-portal (under uid 4003 per S2).
--- phantom-portal
